# Ghostty config (chezmoi-managed: edit in ~/dotfiles, then `chezmoi apply`).
# Note: ~/Library/Application Support/com.mitchellh.ghostty/config is ALSO
# read (after this file, so it wins on conflicts) — keep everything here.

# No Shift+Enter keybind on purpose. Ghostty reports a real Shift+Enter
# (kitty / CSI-u) and tmux forwards it as \e[13;2u (extended-keys csi-u in
# ~/.tmux.conf), so Claude Code and pi both see Shift+Enter = newline. The old
# `shift+enter=text:\x1b\r` rewrite sent Alt+Enter, which pi binds to
# "queue follow-up", so Shift+Enter never inserted a newline there.
